federal officials are investigating a  devastating head-on crash between a bus  and a pickup truck in Texas 13 people  were killed yesterday when the pickup  slammed into the bus carrying church  members home from a retreat only one  person on the bus survived along with  the truck's driver the collision  happened west of San Antonio Omar  Villafranca is at the accident scene in  khon kaen texas omar good morning good  morning the roads down here in this part  of South Texas are two lanes narrow and  curvy the accident happened behind me  about 75 yards right there in the curve  there are still tire marks on the road  the lone survivor in the bus is in  critical condition the driver of the  truck is stable the church members were  coming back from a three-day retreat  when the horrific accident happened the  mangled wreckage is evidence of the  brutal force of the high-speed crash  police say the passenger bus was heading  southbound on highway 83 and the white  pickup truck was driving in the  northbound lane then the truck crossed  the double line hitting the bus head-on  there could have been many contributing  factors we just don't know yet we have  to give the investigators time to look  at everything and then we'll we'll know  exactly what happens the church group  had just left the alto Frio Baptist  encampment in leakey Texas when the  accident happened less than 10 miles  from the campsite police say at first  they did not realize just how tragic of  a wreck they were responding to we're  used to working fatal crash scenes but  first time that we've ever seen  something like this happened with so  many confirmed dead at one time in a  tweet Texas governor Greg Abbott offered  his condolences thank the first  responders who worked the scene and  asked all Texans to offer their thoughts  and prayers their families are going to  be hurting and our church families is  going to be hurting news of the crash  left members of the First Baptist Church  of New Braunfels shell-shocked people  could be seen walking away in tears  church pastor Brad McLane said their  faith is helping them cope with the  devastating loss  together we're just trying to be very  respectful of our families and provide a  place for our church family to come  together  to cry with each other you know to hug  each other pray with each other police  have not released any of the names of  anyone who died there will be grief  counselors at the First Baptist Church  of New Braunfels all week for anyone who  may need it Nora  all right Omar thank you so much
 

